"""Rules text shown in the app and cited by the report."""

RULES = """
This encounter uses a documented subset of the 2024 SRD combat rules. It is not the whole Player's Handbook.

Movement. Each square is 5 feet. A diagonal step costs 5 feet, the same as an orthogonal step. A creature can move through allies and cannot enter an enemy's square. Movement left over can be used before or after the action. Dash is an action and adds the creature's speed. The highest listed speed is used, including fly, because the grid has no altitude.

Actions. A turn has one action and one bonus action, and it ends only when the creature ends it. The action can be an attack, a supported action spell, Dash, Disengage, or Dodge. Attack stays in the menu even when nobody is in reach, and it lists each weapon. Extra Attack keeps that action for a second weapon swing. Dodge imposes disadvantage on attacks against the creature and advantage on its Dexterity saves until its next turn. An imported character can enter Rage, attack recklessly, and spend a bonus-action heal when the public sheet stores that die and its uses.

Bonus actions. A supported bonus-action spell spends the bonus action, not the action. Rage and a sheet heal with a die are bonus actions when the imported character has them. A monster bonus action is resolved when the record has damage dice or a save DC. A Goblin Warrior's Nimble Escape spends the bonus action and is logged as Disengage. It does not add movement or make a stealth roll. Other bonus actions that are only a name and a sentence stay unresolved and are counted.

Attacks. The roll is 1d20 plus the attack bonus against armor class. A natural 20 hits and doubles the dice, not the modifier. A natural 1 misses. A hit from within 5 feet against an unconscious or paralyzed creature is a critical hit. Ranged attacks use the normal range only. A creature can spend its reaction on one melee attack when an enemy leaves its reach, before that step. Disengage prevents it. Sentinel still punishes Disengage and stops a hit creature. Forced movement does not provoke. Weapon mastery can sap, slow, vex, graze, push, topple, cleave, or nick. Push, Tavern Brawler, and Crusher ask before they move the target. When a multiattack sentence says "makes three Rend attacks" and the option count is 1, the sentence count is used. A line that replaces an attack with spellcasting stays unresolved.

Spells. On the battle mat a spell is one choice under Action or Bonus. A creature click resolves a single target. An area spell draws its template under the pointer, and the click resolves it. The engine takes that chosen action in one step when the record, or a short list of description patterns, gives damage or healing and the casting time starts with Action or Bonus Action. The classes are spell attack, saving throw, automatic damage, healing, and a placed zone. Magic missile adds its darts into one roll against the chosen creature, and a higher slot adds darts. Area templates are sphere, cylinder, cube, cone, and line. Cover is ignored, and a sphere includes its center square. Spell slots are spent. Cantrips scale with caster level. Automated casters use the lowest slot that can cast the spell. A spell whose damage waits for a later hit stays excluded. A spell that imposes one of these conditions is resolved. A teleport with no placed template stays excluded.

Saves and damage. A successful save deals half damage when the record or the description says half. If those two disagree, the engine follows the field and the Bestiary counts the disagreement. Resistance halves damage after the save, rounded down. Immunity reduces it to zero. Vulnerability doubles it.

Concentration. The caster maintains one concentration spell. Spirit Guardians and Conjure Woodland Beings follow the caster. A creature saves when that emanation enters its space, when it enters the area, or at the end of its turn, once per turn, and the caster's side is left untouched. A placed zone stays where it was put. Spike Growth deals 2d4 piercing for every 5 feet a creature moves inside it and nothing if the creature stands still. Insect Plague, Cloudkill, Incendiary Cloud, Moonbeam, Black Tentacles, Web, Entangle, Faerie Fire, Call Lightning, and the walls in the 2024 SRD are placed the same way. Cloudkill and Incendiary Cloud drift 10 feet away from the caster at the start of the caster's turn. Call Lightning keeps its cloud and spends the action, not a slot, to call another bolt. A conjured token does not take a turn. That list is Spiritual Weapon, Flaming Sphere, Conjure Animals, Conjure Fey, Conjure Elemental, and Arcane Sword. A new concentration spell, a failed concentration save, or 0 hit points removes the zone or the token. Taking damage forces a Constitution save with DC 10 or half the damage, whichever is higher. Difficult terrain in a zone costs 10 feet per square. Wall of Thorns costs 20 feet per square. Wall of Force, Wall of Stone, and Wall of Ice block the squares they cover. Other self-centered ongoing areas still deal damage when cast and again at the start of the caster's later turns.

Conditions. Blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, grappled, incapacitated, invisible, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, stunned, and unconscious are resolved for players and monsters. A creature at 0 hit points is unconscious and skips its turn. A heal can bring it back. The target repeats the save at the end of its turn when the spell says so. An immunity blocks the condition. Outlined stays the Faerie Fire mark. Grease is difficult terrain and lasts 1 minute without concentration.

Left out on purpose. Cover, beast-form Wild Shape, and anything that only matters on a rest or a skill check. Summon Fey, Dust Devil, and Create Bonfire are not in the 2024 SRD cache. Giant Insect, Summon Dragon, Animate Objects, and Find Familiar need a stat block the monster cache does not have, so those summons stay excluded. An imported Player's Handbook feat is rolled when this fight can resolve it. Epic boons are not rolled. Legendary and lair actions are also omitted. Those records are counted on the Bestiary page instead of being guessed. Imported characters use the weapons, mastery, and structured actions on their public sheet. A Heavy weapon hit adds the proficiency bonus when the sheet's Great Weapon Master action says so.

Enemy tactics. When Rage, Reckless Attack, or a single remaining action is the only real choice, the heuristic acts and the model is not called. Otherwise the model receives a TOON table of the legal attacks, moves, and End turn. The expected number is pressure removed: a hit's damage and the chance it drops the target, or the attacks a condition prevents. A lock is chosen when that beats the hit. The model returns one listed id. A turn can include a move, an action, and a bonus action, so the model may be asked up to six times before the turn is ended. An illegal or unreadable reply is tried once more, then the heuristic's pick is logged as a fallback. The heuristic rages before it attacks when Rage is legal. It then attacks recklessly when Reckless Attack is legal. That choice does not spend the action. It then uses an action spell or attack when one is legal, otherwise moves closer, otherwise Dodges if the action is still unused. A hostile Spirit Guardians or Conjure Woodland Beings area is scored against the hits that move would give up. The creature leaves after attacking when it can still reach, and it stays or enters when those hits can drop the caster first. The heuristic will not leave reach when that swing costs more than the move gains, and it uses a bonus Disengage when that makes leaving safe. In the bonus phase it uses Second Wind, or a bonus heal stored on the sheet, at or below 35 percent hit points, then a bonus spell or attack that deals damage or heals, then ends the turn. It heals an ally at or below 35 percent hit points when that heal uses the budget it is considering. It takes Action Surge once before the attack when an attack is also legal, and the model is not asked for that choice. Push, Tavern Brawler, and Crusher ask before they move the target, and the model is not asked for those choices. When a reaction is triggered, Shield is used if +5 AC would turn a non-critical hit into a miss or if Magic Missile targets the caster, Counterspell is used on an enemy spell that would damage the party or heal a badly wounded enemy unless the Constitution save succeeds even on a natural 1, and Cutting Words is used when its die can turn a hit into a miss or keep an ally above 0 hit points; a hand-played creature is asked instead, and the model is not asked. A monster AC reaction uses the bonus printed on its stat block. Batch fights use that sequence for both sides. Dice in a fight come from a stored seed. Model choices are not seeded.

Round cap. A fight that is still going after 15 rounds is a draw.
""".strip()
